What about **"Confirmation Modal on Stop Generation"**?
If you are generating a 10-hour audiobook, you don't want to accidentally click "Stop Generation" and lose 9.5 hours of work!
Currently, the stop button is:
```tsx
                <button
                  onClick={() => {
                    if (abortController) {
                      abortController.abort();
                      setAbortController(null);
                      setLoading(false);
                      setStatus('Generation stopped by user.');
                    }
                  }}
                  className="w-full py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-white bg-red-500 hover:bg-red-600 shadow-lg flex items-center justify-center gap-2 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5"
                >
                  <Loader2 className="w-5 h-5 animate-spin" /> Stop Generation
                </button>
```

If I change this to:
```tsx
onClick={() => {
    if (window.confirm("Are you sure you want to stop generation? All progress will be lost.")) {
      if (abortController) {
         abortController.abort();
         setAbortController(null);
         setLoading(false);
         setStatus('Generation stopped by user.');
      }
    }
}}
```
This is literally a 3-line change. Very minimal, highly valuable, solves a real problem.
But wait, `window.confirm` is blocking and sometimes frowned upon in modern React apps. A small inline confirmation state would be better.
Click "Stop Generation" -> It changes to "Are you sure? Click to confirm" with a timeout to reset.

