Let's check if there's any other "Stop" logic. No, it's just this one button.

Wait! What if we add a **"Pause/Resume"** feature instead of just Stop?
The Kokoro API in `api/generate/route.ts` runs a `for...of` loop over chunks.
It checks `signal.aborted` to throw an error.
Implementing Pause would require passing a `paused` state to the backend, or the backend holding the loop while `paused` is true. But HTTP SSE requests don't have bidirectional communication to send a "pause" command! You'd have to cancel the request and restart from the last chunk. That's way too complex.
So Two-Step Stop is the best.

